 a bit  both ways but i've definitely become a  lot stricter now with realizing that  there's definitely a type of book that i  would never touch twice and that has  been the majority of books that i've  been reading for the last few years and  that doesn't make me feel too good so um  yeah i'm a bit torn on this one i would  love to hear your thoughts from all the  books i've been rereading um two that i  would definitely recommend are time  enough for love i kind of want to do a  full video on this because it's my  favorite book of all time and also a new  earth or an untethered soul and um short  form is a great place not sponsored  short firm is a great space to kind of  get a summary of these books and see if  they resonate with you if you want to  adapt this framework and then to kind of  invest in actually reading the full  thing which is obviously much more worth  it than anything else now reestablishing  my core knowledge and reasoning as an  adult is something which i feel very  very strongly for and i don't only use  books but i also love to use practical  exercises for for this i love to use  brilliant which are very kindly  sponsoring this video now i am lowkey  obsessed with the little dopamine hits  that i get from the logical questions on  brilliant which kind of i think at least  help me process through books a lot more  quickly and efficiently and if you are  an adult or just a stem student and you  would love to brush up on these  exercises with me there will be a link  in my description which will give you a  free trial or a discount depending on  what you want to do with it so yeah  thank you so much if you made it so far  i hope you have a wonderful rest of your  day be count yourself on others and  don't believe everything you think  thanks bye
 

